    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d658">

                <pb facs="0622" n="538" sameAs="frus:frus1918Supp02/pg538"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 867.48/542</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Ambassador in Turkey</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Elkus</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1917-02-15T16:00:00-05:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">February 15, 1917, 4 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>3352. Your 2457.<anchor n="4" xml:id="d658-f1"/> Prior to severing diplomatic
                    relations with Germany, Department had desired consent of Turkish Government <pb
                        facs="0623" n="539" xml:id="pg539"/> for <hi rendition="#italic">Caesar</hi>
                    to enter Mersine. Both <hi rendition="#italic">Des Moines</hi> and <hi
                        rendition="#italic">Caesar</hi>, however, have been ordered to remain
                    Alexandria until further notice.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Lansing</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
